ARCHITECTURE (mirrors the A7 RegenEfficiency / SharedDrive precedents)
  MediaPlayerPageModel.kt      framework-free: registration ids; parseLatestMedia /
                               parseMediaHistory (decode GET /media/latest + GET /media,
                               null/empty guards = web `latest?` / `history?.length`);
                               the verbatim ports of the web useMemo chain — mediaStats
                               (web `stats`), volumePoints (web `volumeChartData`),
                               sourceSlices (web `sourceData`), mediaProgressPercent
                               (web `progressPct`), volumeMaxOf (web `|| 11`),
                               formatPlayTime (web `fmtPlayTime`), MediaStatusKind
                               (web statusVariant/statusLabel); MediaPlayerDisplayPrefs
                               (web fmtInt/fmtNumber, locale-aware, no SI math — volume
                               is a raw device scale); recordMediaPlayerPageOpened
                               (view.opened); mapData.
  MediaPlayerPageSource.kt     seam over the shared resilient ApiHttpClient.safeRequest
                               for `/media/latest` + `/media?limit=500` (web inline
                               request() reads; no media S7 repo exists, same as the
                               SharedDrive/TemperatureImpact inline-read precedent) +
                               SelectedVehicleStore (web useSelectedVehicle) +
                               SettingsStore.settings (web useFormatting).
  MediaPlayerPageViewModel.kt  BaseFeedViewModel; latestState: StateFlow<UiState<
                               MediaSnapshot?>> re-collected on vehicle/refresh, gated on
                               the active vehicle, empty when the decode is null (web
                               `latest?`); historyState: StateFlow<UiState<List<
                               MediaSnapshot>>>; displayPrefs StateFlow; refresh/retry/
                               recordViewOpened. No HTTP in the view.
  MediaPlayerPage.kt           stateless MediaPlayerPageContent + the nine Material 3
                               panels; the latest snapshot drives the now-playing card +
                               the volume gauge, the history feed is folded by the model
                               into the four metric cards, the two charts, and the table.
  MediaPlayerPageHost.kt       registers MediaPlayerRoute for the `mediaPlayer`
                               destination (Destinations.kt L109, /media-player); wired in
                               TeslaSyncApplication.onCreate() (NavHost registration).

SI BOUNDARY (P1/S5)
  This surface carries no SI quantity: audio volume is a raw device scale (0..max), the
  counts are integers, and the play position is milliseconds formatted as m:ss. The only
  render-boundary formatting is the locale-aware fmtInt/fmtNumber port in
  MediaPlayerDisplayPrefs (web useFormatting); nothing is stored converted.

LIVE DATA / STALENESS (ADR-013)
  Neither feed is an SSE live stream; both are cache-then-network Resource streams
  projected to UiState (the web page polls /media/latest every 10s via refetchInterval —
  the native refresh() trigger is the analogue), so the header DataFreshness chip surfaces
  fetchedAt / refreshing / stale / error rather than a >2 min live-staleness badge.

